# Do not touch fixture line endings.
#
# The golden fixtures are byte-sensitive: tests compare the exact JSON bytes,
# and the sync engine's canonical serialisation depends on exact numeric
# formatting. Git's CRLF conversion on checkout would silently break them on
# Windows, which is where most contributors will clone.
fixtures/** -text

# Everything else: normalise to LF, both in the repository and on checkout.
# `text=auto` alone only normalises the repository copy; adding `eol=lf` also
# checks out LF, so source stays byte-identical on Windows and on POSIX.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Windows batch files must keep CRLF, or cmd.exe misreads blocks and labels.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
